# Eta reduction:  λx.(M x) -> M   provided x is not free in M.
# Run with -e; without it every line below is already in normal form.

λx.(f x)
λx.λy.(x y)
λf.λx.(f x)
λx.λy.((f x) y)

# The side condition is the whole rule.  In both of these x IS free in M, so
# the abstraction uses its argument and the binder cannot be discarded.
λx.(x x)
λx.((f x) x)

# Not an eta-redex at all: the argument is not the binder.
λx.(f y)

# The alpha-renamed binder from the capture test is an eta-redex, which is
# exactly why eta is off by default -- it would erase the evidence.
λy1.(y y1)

# Eta fires before beta here: the body is an application whose argument is
# the binder, and (λy.y) does not mention x.
λx.(λy.y x)

# Beta first, then nothing left to eta-reduce.
(λx.(f x) g)
